config KSHRINK_SLABD
	bool "Enable asynchronous slab shrinker daemon"
	default n
	help
	  Move slab shrinking out of the direct-reclaim path and into a
	  background kthread.  When direct reclaim wants to shrink slab
	  caches, it wakes kshrink_slabd instead of calling shrink_slab()
	  synchronously; the daemon runs the shrinker work on a CPU that
	  is not the highest-frequency CPU.

	  This can reduce allocation latency for the caller at the cost
	  of doing the slab reclaim asynchronously.  The daemon is
	  started at boot and only runs when woken.

	  Say Y here to enable the asynchronous slab shrinker daemon.
	  If unsure, say N.
